  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA shortwave/low pressure system will lift northeast along the \nAtlantic coast later today and Sunday. Moisture from this will \ncreate precipitation, mainly across the mountainous counties later \ntonight and on Sunday, although models have backed off somewhat\nwith the westward extent of precipitation shield. In addition, \na trough and associated cold front will approach from the west, \nspreading light precipitation into the area for late Sunday \nnight into Monday, along with cooler temperatures to start next \nweek. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nForecast becomes increasingly uncertain for mid to late next week, \nbut general consensus is for well defined shortwaves, one across the \nSouthern Plains, and another that will dig southeast out of the \nUpper Midwest into the Mid Mississippi Valley region, with the two \neventually phasing and moving east across the area. Quite a bit of \nuncertainty remains in the exact path and evolution, and thus, \nprecipitation types/amounts/impacts. As of now, most of the \nprecipitation should fall as rain, but there could be brief wintry \nmix periods across the mountains at times depending on which model \nends up being correct.",
